        <fma:definition>Material anatomical entity which is generated by coordinated expression of the organism&apos;s own genes that guide its morphogenesis; has inherent 3D shape; its parts are connected and spatially related to one another in patterns determined by coordinated gene expression. Examples: embryo, mesoderm, heart, right ventricle, mitral valve, myocardium, endothelium, lymphocyte, fibroblast, thorax, cardiovascular system, hemoglobin, T cell receptor.</fma:definition>
